{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>A sacred linen tunic</b> etc. And why does it say <b>bad</b> (linen) four times? To exclude the ephod and breastplate and robe and tzitz, for the priest does not enter with them לפני ולפנים, even though it is said of all of them לפני ה'." "<b>Upon his flesh.</b> A euphemism for nakedness, like <b>זב מבשרו</b>. Why does it say ילבש, יחגור, יצנוף? Since in the end it includes other garments for him between the afternoons — when he has none, how can he not don [them] in the morning? Scripture says ילבש, יחגור, יצנוף." "<b>And with a linen turban he shall wrap.</b> The ephod and breastplate are not mentioned; from this they learned that in the Second Temple they would serve without Urim and Thummim." "<b>They are sacred garments.</b> A general principle for all garments — that they must be of sacred property." "<b>And he shall wash his flesh in water.</b> Rashi: that day requires immersion for every change of garments, etc. It is the way of the world for one who serves before the king to wash his flesh and purify himself each time; and since they are served by attendants, we are concerned lest he touched something unclean and will go back and defile the garments — therefore Scripture required for every donning and removing: sanctification of hands and feet. As we derive in Yoma, since Scripture casts ורחץ את בשרו במים between ופשט and לבש, to give washing for removing, and washing for donning. For if it is not needed for immersion — which we derive from <b>ורחץ במים את בשרו ולבשם</b> — assign it to the matter of washing hands. And what Rashi explained, 'sanctification of hands and feet from the basin' — that is from the water in the basin, for we hold in the Mishnah: he drew [water] from the bowl, that day he sanctifies his hands and feet from a golden flask."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {1 "The phrase בין הערבים (between the evenings) appears to stand for the afternoon service; the argument's logic is compressed and the reading is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:12:45.789297903Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}